+# U2 proposed delivery packet: one selected task across clients
+
+Prepared 2026-11-13 by U1 for root review. **Undispatched and unapproved.**
+U1 worker completion is not architectural acceptance, U2 implementation authority
+or an extension of U1's $40 envelope. Root selects its cost envelope, builder,
+reviewer, current inputs and file claims before launch.
+
+Deliver one coherent operator journey: CLI, TUI and authenticated browser select
+the same explicit endpoint/task, show owner objective, question/result and
+independent execution observations, and inspect owner-linked session activity
+without retargeting selection. Start with the controlled subject in the
+[U1 source map](../records/unified-operator-interface-u1-source-map-20261113.md).
+Its retained task evidence and newly parsed session are different observations;
+U2 must visibly identify fixture/replay versus a fresh installed-host read.
+
+## Preconditions and exact contracts
+
+Root first accepts an exact U1 source/map/qualification subject after separate
+Astra xhigh architecture review. Preserve the
+[U1 budget's architectural-risk contract](unified-operator-interface-u1-budget-20261113.md):
+first serious independent rejection warns and permits bounded repair; second
+rejection after repair in the affected subsystem blocks ordinary repair for
+separate design review; serious repair regression or recurring invariant
+violation escalates immediately. Inherited boundary evidence counts. Infra
+interruptions neither count nor reset history. Root owns the ledger and gate.
+
+The accepted causal-observability design owns observed/derived/interpreted
+classes, confidentiality and absence of UI workflow authority. TO2 owns
+`task.observe.v2`, its five independent components, six states, exact scopes,
+identity fencing, native completeness/capacity and missing task-command edge.
+`lifecycle-wire` remains the shared domain-value validator; the existing TUI
+read/decoder/anchor behavior is implementation material, not a competing owner.
+Session-query owns argument, protected-file, source digest and native read
+semantics. `work-engine.operator-observation.v1` remains an explicitly bounded
+session projection consumed by existing clients. Its successful read time is
+not task freshness or event time.
+
+The final prerequisite digest table below binds the U1-prepared revisions.
+Before U2 dispatch, root refreshes changed assumptions and supplies accepted
+subject references; changing a hash alone cannot refresh a semantic claim.
+No new contract is assumed settled by owner acknowledgements, board request
+5172 or an unaccepted research artifact.
+
+## Controlled and production standing
+
+The starting identity is `task:ui:sim` / `subject:s8:task`, with retained owner
+revision 4 and lifecycle cursor 32 at the exact historical store/stream in U1.
+Its native segment joins via `input:command:ui:sim`, then selected delivery,
+thread `01a142ba-b70b-7eb0-9900-b53bece80f30` and turn
+`01a142ba-b722-7272-affc-928d3a20aeed`. Titles, paths, timestamp proximity and
+transcript phrases cannot establish these edges. Subject equality alone is
+insufficient for a task sharing a subject. Missing or conflicting owner-backed
+input/native linkage remains unlinked.
+
+The selected current Events owner is SHA-256
+`586128d82ebd1fa0c8813e5583924cd9ce812e6ffe76de0c2e63d396414e2a8b`.
+Use only the actual U1-qualified scope/disposition recorded in its result.
+There is no selected production profile, authenticated remote connector proof,
+provider activation or live deployment. Granted-operation fixture standing and
+its resolved secure-path environment interruption must remain distinct from
+bridge-null monitor qualification. Root approved a private fixture route only;
+that is not permission to weaken secure-path checks or activate a domain. No real credentials or production endpoints are reused.
+
+For a fresh installed controlled-host proof, root must bind an existing trusted
+host build/startup template, immutable source/lock/toolchain pins and a finite
+provider-disabled simulator, plus authorize its private fixture process scope.
+The old captured response is not a substitute for that fresh proof. No
+production grant, mutation or paid provider is authorized by this packet.
+
+## Bounded implementation outcome and ownership
+
+One builder should own the shared read and all three consumer changes, so DTO,
+identity and stale-state meaning cannot drift between independent assignments.
+The Rust boundary composes existing read contracts and presentation references;
+it does not become a task, lifecycle, review, limit or scheduler owner.
+
+Proposed file scope, subject to root's precise packet/claims:
+
+- `rust/crates/operator-observation/`: smallest shared Rust task-read/projection
+  surface needed for this selected journey and CLI. Reuse/extract the public
+  TO2 read/decoder/anchor behavior with existing lifecycle-wire validators.
+  Settle exact public type/wire boundaries in the implementation plan after
+  architecture acceptance; no generic workflow schema, event database or
+  persistent service is required by U2.
+- `rust/crates/terminal-ui/`: consume the shared read/identity/anchor semantics,
+  preserve drafts/inspection/selection, and keep its read-only behavior. Moving
+  reusable code must preserve its existing identity/deadline/late-reply tests.
+- Sibling `/home/bline/code/devwits-auth`: existing authenticated mailbox adapter,
+  activity/selected-task view and tests only, after explicit root ownership.
+  Browser JavaScript consumes Rust-produced bounded projections; it does not
+  independently reinterpret TO2 owner payloads or recreate joins.
+- Component docs, exact shared fixtures and bounded U2 qualification records.
+  Any Cargo dependency/lock delta is proposed and root-owned before mutation;
+  preserve concurrent entries. No task-host/lifecycle/research source repair,
+  grants, provider activation, installation, deployment or commit authority.
+
+Process scope: private build targets, finite unit/fixture tests, one owned
+controlled installed host/simulator where authorized, and actual CLI/TUI/browser
+qualification processes. Use worker custody with explicit input digests and
+frozen dirty baselines; retain failures/fixtures and reap every owned process.
+No persistent collector, sync daemon or listener is installed. Root owns result
+collection and separate review dispatch; no worker spawns paid work.
+
+## Required behavior and validation
+
+Use explicit endpoint plus task ID and retain that selection through refresh
+and drill-down. Keep owner objective separate from operator navigation label.
+Show task question/result, lifecycle/native state and linked session activity
+with each source's class, scope, revision/cutoff and age. Show read failure,
+refusal, known absence, known empty and not-requested states distinctly. Retain
+last-known values only with their original verified scopes/ages; invalidate on
+endpoint/host/account/source/established identity changes. Fence old selection
+generation replies. Do not merge independent reads into an atomic workflow cut.
+
+Validate the same Rust-produced owner records through all clients with:
+
+- Positive exact task→input→native→session linkage, plus conflicting task,
+  subject, input, native thread and source-profile controls. Unlinked activity
+  stays unlinked. Events entries have no structured per-turn join.
+- Owner absence, failure/refusal, unchanged and changed host identities, partial
+  independent components, source failure, reconnect and late/out-of-order
+  replies. Known-empty native collections remain distinct from the 65-row
+  capacity refusal. No command/task edge appears from a selected command ID.
+- A task answer/result changing without transcript activity, independent
+  lifecycle/native changes, and consumer-clock age transition without a record
+  change. Each uses its own read/reconciliation route; a healthy Events stream
+  cannot renew other owners' freshness.
+- Actual CLI output and one TUI/browser selected-work journey through detail and
+  back. Include desktop/phone frames, sign-out/account-change clearing,
+  authentication failure and confidentiality/redaction controls. Mocked remote
+  transport and a fresh installed controlled host are labeled separately.
+
+U2 can use explicit reconciliation polling in its controlled environment, with
+its cadence and read duration visible. Notification/replay delivery, all-owner
+recovery and the proposed five-second source-to-render target belong to U3/U4
+qualification. Do not claim that target from API acknowledgement, mailbox fetch
+or historical UI screen waits. Readiness may be bounded when campaign/review/
+limits/scheduler associations are unavailable; those dimensions remain visibly
+unestablished, not zero or empty.
+
+## Return and acceptance boundary
+
+Return exact source/dirty-baseline delta, owner/build/schema/profile/fixture
+pins, validation and rendered evidence, supported/missing joins, per-owner
+refresh routes and explicit process disposition. Root obtains independent
+review, applies inherited risk history, and decides bounded acceptance and
+integration. Full UI-0–UI-4, S5 causal reconstruction, economics/recommendations,
+an atomic cut, production qualification and deployment remain outside U2.
+
